  "text": "CapCut vs Premiere Pro: does anyone actually need Adobe Premiere for short-form video? Paying sixty dollars monthly for crashing timelines and slow proxy rendering burns out solo creators. Premiere demands manual keyframing, nested sequences, and sluggish Media Encoder exports for basic vertical clips. CapCut automates kinetic captions, smart background cutouts, and dynamic zooms right on your timeline. You ship client reels twice as fast.",
